#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# euclidean_distance

#% text
# `euclidean_distance(u, v)` gives the Euclidean distance between the vectors `u` and `v`.

#% section
# Details

#% item
# The distance is `sqrt(abs(u1 - v1)^2 + abs(u2 - v2)^2 + ...)`; coordinates that agree are left out, so a single difference gives `abs(u_i - v_i)`.

#% item
# For numbers it is `abs(u - v)`.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
euclidean_distance([a, b], [a, c])
#% output
#= abs(b - c)

#% cell
euclidean_distance([1, 2, 3], [2, 4, 6])
#% output
#= 14^(1/2)

#% cell
euclidean_distance([a, b, c], [x, y, z])
#% output
#= (abs(a - x)^2 + abs(b - y)^2 + abs(c - z)^2)^(1/2)

#% cell
euclidean_distance([1., 5., 2.], [4., 15., 18.])
#% output
#= 19.1049731745428

#% cell
euclidean_distance(3, 7)
#% output
#= 4

#% section
# See also

#% text
# `norm`, `hamming_distance`
